      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Washington Mills-Mayodan Plant earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 2005, honoring its industrial heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayodan%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mayodan’s origins trace back to 1892 when a cotton mill was built, launching the town’s mill‑town era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayodan%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Washington Mills Company, later known as Tultex, operated a textile mill in Mayodan until 1999, marking the end of an era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayodan%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today, Mayodan hosts the manufacturing plant of Sturm, Ruger & Co., a major firearms producer with a long history in the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
